;   Inspect — the cast entry for spell slot 27 (issue #3).
;
;   The slot's init used to be the one-byte `rts` at $9112. The next byte,
;   $9113, is `pha` and is called by other spells (`jsr $9113` from the
;   featherlite path), so the rts cannot be overwritten with a longer
;   instruction. SPSLOT.PDS retargets the init vector here instead.
;
;   The call is `jmp (t0)` (the dispatcher at slot 0 $8F39), so `rts` returns
;   to the dispatcher's caller, which is what the old rts did. T2 is the
;   power level 1..4, T3 the spell number, T4 the caster (x2.pds's spell-init
;   header). This entry does not read them yet: a cast of slot 27 still does
;   what the cartridge did, which is return. The body lands here once the
;   drawing layer is actually called from the game.
;
;   IN:  as the spell init the vector calls (jmp indirect, so rts exits it)
;   OUT: A, X, Y preserved
;   USES: nothing
;
;   Written by us. Eurocom's source is read-only and pinned; see README.md.

        org $fb47
obinspect rts
